\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces One HDET fan-out/converge cycle with $N{=}4$ replicas and spread ratio $\alpha $. All replicas share the same all-reduced gradient at each step but take steps of different sizes, causing parameters to diverge. Every $T$ steps an AllReduce average collapses the ensemble into a single model. Learning rates are randomly reassigned (reshuffled) before the next cycle. }}{4}{figure.1}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:cycle}{{1}{4}{One HDET fan-out/converge cycle with $N{=}4$ replicas and spread ratio $\alpha $. All replicas share the same all-reduced gradient at each step but take steps of different sizes, causing parameters to diverge. Every $T$ steps an AllReduce average collapses the ensemble into a single model. Learning rates are randomly reassigned (reshuffled) before the next cycle}{figure.1}{}}
